install/
log/
.colcon/

# Campaign output.
#
# `results/*` rather than `results/`: git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so a trailing-slash exclusion makes every negation below it dead
# text. The distinction is invisible until you need it.
#
# What is tracked is the evidence a reader needs to check a claim: the integrity
# baseline, the comparator campaigns the paper reports, their logs, and the
# configuration sweeps.
#
# The sweeps were excluded on size once. That was wrong, and the rule it broke
# is a pre-registered one: COMPARATOR_SPEC R8 requires the complete sweep table
# to be *published*, best to worst, precisely so that "the baseline was weak"
# can be checked by a reader instead of answered by assurance. It is the single
# artefact that answers the strongest available criticism of this work, and 5 MB
# is not a reason to withhold it.
results/*
!results/PRE_CAMPAIGN_BASELINE.sha256
!results/DEVELOPMENT_NORMALISERS.json
!results/campaign_v5.csv
!results/campaign_v5.log
!results/held_out.csv
!results/held_out.log
!results/static_sweep_development_v5.csv
!results/static_sweep_held_out.csv
campaigns/

# `static_sweep.csv` itself is deliberately NOT tracked: it is the path the
# campaign runner writes to, so whichever campaign ran last owns it. The named
# snapshots above are what get published, so that a file in the repository can
# never be ambiguous about which campaign produced it.
results/static_sweep.csv
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
*.json.gz

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
